---Describes the data disk used by a workflow job.
---@class gcp.dataflow_v1b3.Disk
---@field mountPoint? string Directory in a VM where disk is mounted.
---@field diskType? string Disk storage type, as defined by Google Compute Engine. This must be a disk type appropriate to the project and zone in which the workers will run. If unknown or unspecified, the service will attempt to choose a reasonable default. For example, the standard persistent disk type is a resource name typically ending in "pd-standard". If SSD persistent disks are available, the resource name typically ends with "pd-ssd". The actual valid values are defined the Google Compute Engine API, not by the Cloud Dataflow API; consult the Google Compute Engine documentation for more information about determining the set of available disk types for a particular project and zone. Google Compute Engine Disk types are local to a particular project in a particular zone, and so the resource name will typically look something like this: compute.googleapis.com/projects/project-id/zones/zone/diskTypes/pd-standard
---@field sizeGb? number Size of disk in GB. If zero or unspecified, the service will attempt to choose a reasonable default.

---@alias gcp.dataflow_v1b3.DiskList gcp.dataflow_v1b3.Disk[]

---Data provided with a pipeline or transform to provide descriptive info.
---@class gcp.dataflow_v1b3.DisplayData
---@field int64Value? string Contains value if the data is of int64 type.
---@field javaClassValue? string Contains value if the data is of java class type.
---@field key? string The key identifying the display data. This is intended to be used as a label for the display data when viewed in a dax monitoring system.
---@field label? string An optional label to display in a dax UI for the element.
---@field namespace? string The namespace for the key. This is usually a class name or programming language namespace (i.e. python module) which defines the display data. This allows a dax monitoring system to specially handle the data and perform custom rendering.
---@field strValue? string Contains value if the data is of string type.
---@field boolValue? boolean Contains value if the data is of a boolean type.
---@field url? string An optional full URL.
---@field floatValue? number Contains value if the data is of float type.
---@field timestampValue? string Contains value if the data is of timestamp type.
---@field durationValue? string Contains value if the data is of duration type.
---@field shortStrValue? string A possible additional shorter value to display. For example a java_class_name_value of com.mypackage.MyDoFn will be stored with MyDoFn as the short_str_value and com.mypackage.MyDoFn as the java_class_name value. short_str_value can be displayed and java_class_name_value will be displayed as a tooltip.

---@alias gcp.dataflow_v1b3.DisplayDataList gcp.dataflow_v1b3.DisplayData[]

---A metric value representing a distribution.
---@class gcp.dataflow_v1b3.DistributionUpdate
---@field max? gcp.dataflow_v1b3.SplitInt64 The maximum value present in the distribution.
---@field sum? gcp.dataflow_v1b3.SplitInt64 Use an int64 since we'd prefer the added precision. If overflow is a common problem we can detect it and use an additional int64 or a double.
---@field count? gcp.dataflow_v1b3.SplitInt64 The count of the number of elements present in the distribution.
---@field min? gcp.dataflow_v1b3.SplitInt64 The minimum value present in the distribution.
---@field histogram? gcp.dataflow_v1b3.Histogram (Optional) Histogram of value counts for the distribution.
---@field sumOfSquares? number Use a double since the sum of squares is likely to overflow int64.

