---Hints for splitting a Source into bundles (parts for parallel processing) using SourceSplitRequest.
---@class gcp.dataflow_v1b3.SourceSplitOptions
---@field desiredBundleSizeBytes? string The source should be split into a set of bundles where the estimated size of each is approximately this many bytes.
---@field desiredShardSizeBytes? string DEPRECATED in favor of desired_bundle_size_bytes.

---Represents the operation to split a high-level Source specification into bundles (parts for parallel processing). At a high level, splitting of a source into bundles happens as follows: SourceSplitRequest is applied to the source. If it returns SOURCE_SPLIT_OUTCOME_USE_CURRENT, no further splitting happens and the source is used "as is". Otherwise, splitting is applied recursively to each produced DerivedSource. As an optimization, for any Source, if its does_not_need_splitting is true, the framework assumes that splitting this source would return SOURCE_SPLIT_OUTCOME_USE_CURRENT, and doesn't initiate a SourceSplitRequest. This applies both to the initial source being split and to bundles produced from it.
---@class gcp.dataflow_v1b3.SourceSplitRequest
---@field source? gcp.dataflow_v1b3.Source Specification of the source to be split.
---@field options? gcp.dataflow_v1b3.SourceSplitOptions Hints for tuning the splitting process.

---The response to a SourceSplitRequest.
---@class gcp.dataflow_v1b3.SourceSplitResponse
---@field shards? gcp.dataflow_v1b3.SourceSplitShardList DEPRECATED in favor of bundles.
---@field outcome? gcp.dataflow_v1b3.SourceSplitResponseOutcomeEnum|string Indicates whether splitting happened and produced a list of bundles. If this is USE_CURRENT_SOURCE_AS_IS, the current source should be processed "as is" without splitting. "bundles" is ignored in this case. If this is SPLITTING_HAPPENED, then "bundles" contains a list of bundles into which the source was split.
---@field bundles? gcp.dataflow_v1b3.DerivedSourceList If outcome is SPLITTING_HAPPENED, then this is a list of bundles into which the source was split. Otherwise this field is ignored. This list can be empty, which means the source represents an empty input.

---@alias gcp.dataflow_v1b3.SourceSplitResponseOutcomeEnum "SOURCE_SPLIT_OUTCOME_UNKNOWN"|"SOURCE_SPLIT_OUTCOME_USE_CURRENT"|"SOURCE_SPLIT_OUTCOME_SPLITTING_HAPPENED"

---DEPRECATED in favor of DerivedSource.
---@class gcp.dataflow_v1b3.SourceSplitShard
